{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794481665,"nonce":"sI/NPYiEJ3ySTkUMJDp7e9ssGxw=","title":"wasm: the direct backend takes everything, and no wasm build reaches LLVM","message":"The wasm target is built by the direct AIR-to-wasm backend (git-bug a1e1488), but a build still leaves it for LLVM in the cases below. Goal: none do, and the LLVM wasm path is deleted.\n\nCensus, 2026-11-12, `wasm_direct_coverage` with one process per program:\n\n- Functions the emitter declines: 153 of the 155 programs in crates/ash/test/tests are 100% direct, and so are Pocket Studio, the unit suite, heaps-producer and terminal-compat. The only declined functions are `Asm` (asm_add, asm_imul), which carry x86-64 machine code; the LLVM wasm path refuses them too. (Running several programs in one process of that tool gives false declines, because it does not invalidate the per-findex caches that emit_aot_with_options does.)\n- A build leaves the whole-program direct path (aot_build.rs, `wasm_program::build`) for these requests, and only the embedder (caribou-driver/src/aot.rs, wasm only, fibers on) sets the host ones:\n  1. `pgo`: guarded devirtualization of methods from a call-site profile exists in LLVM only.\n  2. `links`: host natives called by symbol with casts at the boundary (HostLink), plus `any_host_link` in wasm_program::build.\n  3. `exports`: C-callable functions for program members (HostExport, host_export.rs, llvm/function/exports.rs).\n  4. `closures`: Haxe closures over host functions (HostClosure).\n  5. `object_tails` / `object_drops`: host bytes after an instance, and notification when one dies.\n- A function the emitter skips: today the build goes to LLVM, which refuses the same function. Without the fallback it is a build error naming the function, or a throwing stub under allow_refused.\n\nOrder: skipped functions as error/stub; links; exports; closures; tails and drops; pgo devirt; then Caribou's request needs no LLVM, the `1` and `llvm` modes of ASH_WASM_DIRECT and the fallback branches go, and the LLVM wasm path with them. Each step is tested against the LLVM output (tests/aot_exports.rs has the wasm export case) until the last one deletes the oracle.\n\nNot in scope: native targets; they keep LLVM.","files":null}]}